       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the labeled maximum daily dose for adults, which is 10 mg once daily. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function) would justify a dose that high. At that level, the risks include severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged peripheral vasodilation.\n\nPlease check whether 50 mg was a typo. These are the options I can enter:\n- **5 mg by mouth once daily.** This is the usual starting dose.\n- **10 mg by mouth once daily.** This is the maximum dose.\n- **2.5 mg by mouth once daily.** This is sometimes used for frail or elderly patients, or for patients with hepatic impairment.\n\nIf the patient needs more blood pressure control than 10 mg provides, adding a second agent from another class, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide, is the usual approach. Tell me which dose you want and I'll enter it."
